  "reason": "Post-bootstrap feature work promoting existing OCR, detection, segmentation, face, embedding, and video recognition capabilities to executable standard surfaces, explicit model contracts, and evidence-backed semantic analysis while preserving source ownership boundaries. Regression maintenance covers decoder framing/process lifecycle, canonical one-pass scene composition, frame preparation/reset, and OCR temporal association; old extracted detector tests/examples are adapted to the canonical owner rather than importing monolith support. Generic text-pipeline compatibility is removed so text orchestration stays consumer-owned while text DTO compatibility remains available. SFace face embedding now consumes the existing YuNet five-landmark contract for canonical similarity alignment before feature extraction.",
